From ca3b3e42eb076bf925d8a434eb8b81da7febb91c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:53:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: Dolby Vision Standard tunnel on DCE 11.2 and
 12

amdgpu_dm offered DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB only on the DCN pipelines it was
reviewed for (amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dcn_reviewed()). With the display core
carrying the bytes of a byte tunnel stream on DCE (the patch before), it is
offered on DCE 11.2 (Polaris), 11.22 (Vega M) and 12.0 and 12.1 (Vega 10, 12
and 20) too. amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_reviewed() goes through the pipe block by
block: memory input, input pixel processor, DCP, line buffer and scaler,
formatter, stream encoder (the AVI InfoFrame in its own registers, the Dolby
VSIF in generic packet 0, which sends 28 bytes after its header: the 27 of
the VSIF and the checksum) and sequencer.

Polaris runs the same display code as Vega M: the same dce112 pool, clock
manager and blocks. CroqueMr's fork offers the tunnel on Vega M alone
("not Polaris DCE11.2"), but nothing in the code tells the two apart.
DCE 12 differs from DCE 11.2 in its timing generator (timing, blank and
overscan colours, a DP test pattern) and in the GFX9 tiling and watermarks
of its memory input, none of which touch a pixel of the plane. Not DCE 11.0
and older: HDMI up to 300 MHz (297 on DCE 8 and 6), the underlay pipe and FBC
of DCE 11.0 not reviewed, and DCE 6 cannot set the depth of its line buffer.

Fail-closed, and saying what it found:

- once dc_validate_global_state() has validated the context,
  amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_check_dce() reads from it what DC will program for the
  pipe of each tunnelled stream on DCE (amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce_pipe_why()):
  one pipe with the plane, no second plane or ODM pipe, the graphics input
  CSC listed, the line buffer at 24 bpp, the scaler at 1:1 with one tap over
  the whole raster, the bit depth reduction of DITHER_OPTION_TRUN8 and no
  clamp in the formatter. Anything else refuses the commit, as "scanout" in
  DVBRIDGE_REFUSED and in the kernel log with the reason
  (amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_refused_dce()); user space keeps the display as it
  was and plays HDR10;
- each time the tunnel goes on (a modeset of a tunnelled stream), the
  registers of its pipe are read back (dc_stream_read_byte_tunnel()) into
  the kernel log, with what is not as the tunnel needs it
  (amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce_readback_why()), the mode in which the graphics
  input CSC was found, and what the VBIOS lets the HDMI encoder send
  (HDMI_6GB_EN: without it 2160p50 and 2160p60 are not validated, and the
  player is not offered them).

What already covered DCE through the version numbers says so now: the
legacy gamma refused before DCN 3 (DCE has the input gamma LUT of DCN 1) and
the output transfer function refused at commit setup (the regamma of DCE has
an sRGB mode).

Host test: amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce_pipe_why() and
amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce_readback_why(), cut out of this file and built on the
display core's own headers, accept the pipe that the display core builds for
a 2160p tunnel on DCE 11.2, 11.22, 12.0 and 12.1 and refuse 14 changes of it,
each naming the reason; the read back of that pipe passes, and an input CSC
turned on after the tunnel, a line buffer at 30 bpp, an output CSC and a
dithering formatter are found in it. Not verified: anything on a DCE machine
with a Dolby Vision TV.
